It keeps a hash closing against the output tag delimiter intact
{{ form_widget(form.message, {'attr': {'rows': 3}}) }}

It keeps a bare nested hash intact
{{ {'a': {'b': 1}} }}

It keeps a nested hash passed to a filter intact
{{ foo|default({'a': {'b': 1}}) }}

It keeps a nested hash passed to include intact
{{ include('partial.html.twig', {'attrs': {'class': 'foo'}}) }}

It keeps three levels of nesting intact
{{ dump({'a': {'b': {'c': 1}}}) }}

It does not insert a whitespace marker inside a breaking expression
<div>
  {{ form_widget(form.message, {'attr': {'rows': 3, 'class': 'form-control something long enough to force a break'}}) }}
</div>

It keeps following text out of the expression
<div>{{ attrs({'data': {'x': 1}}) }} trailing text</div>

It handles a nested hash inside an html attribute
<div class="{{ classes({'a': {'b': 1}}) }}"></div>

It keeps a nested array intact
{{ foo([1, [2, 3]]) }}

It keeps a string containing the output tag delimiter intact
{{ 'a }} b' }}

It keeps a quote nested in a string of the other style intact
{{ trans({'%name%': "it's here"}) }}

It preserves whitespace control operators around a nested hash
{{- foo({'a': {'b': 1}}) -}}
{{~ foo({'a': {'b': 1}}) ~}}

It leaves an unterminated quote alone rather than swallowing the doc
{{ it's }}
<div>{{ 'x' }}</div>
